{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.535,
   "text": "The lake had one rule for lifeguards. It was painted on the back of my chair."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.135,
   "end": 15.385,
   "text": "Count the swimmers at sunset. If the number goes up by one... clear the water. Never count again."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.185,
   "end": 21.241,
   "text": "All summer, the numbers matched. I figured it was an old joke for new guards."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.941,
   "end": 27.36,
   "text": "Then, on the last night of August, I counted eleven heads bobbing in the dark water."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.96,
   "end": 30.349,
   "text": "I counted again. Twelve."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.349,
   "end": 37.512,
   "text": "I blew the whistle. Everyone swam in, laughing, complaining about the cold."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 38.212,
   "end": 41.348,
   "text": "Eleven people stood dripping on the sand."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 42.348,
   "end": 47.34,
   "text": "Out past the rope, one dark head stayed above the water... perfectly still."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 49.34,
   "end": 52.839,
   "text": "It didn't swim. It didn't sink. It just watched me."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 53.839,
   "end": 57.209,
   "text": "Then it slipped under... without a single ripple."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.809,
   "end": 62.799,
   "text": "And I broke the rule. I counted the beach one more time."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 63.999,
   "end": 64.878,
   "text": "Twelve."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 67.278,
   "end": 70.841,
   "text": "Eleven of them were shivering in the cold night air."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 71.841,
   "end": 76.534,
   "text": "One of them wasn't. It just smiled at me... and asked for a ride home."
  }
 ],
